Hmm, indeed. The test below doesn't call proto.\[[Set]], and just calls the setter. Should I just add a check for `[OverrideBuiltins]`?

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<script>
var ds = document.documentElement.dataset;
var a = new Proxy(Object.getPrototypeOf(ds), {
  set(...args) { w(args); return false; },
});
Object.setPrototypeOf(ds, a);
ds.x = "foo";
w(ds.x)
</script>
```

<del>It also turns out WebKit isn't following the spec for the non-`[OverrideBuiltins]` case; it was just messing with my `__proto__` set. Updated the result in https://github.com/heycam/webidl/issues/630#issue-402192460.</del>
